Seven process arcs of 2026-08-27 stood at verdict OPEN: B1171, B1172, B1173, B1176, B1177, B1178 and B1179. Main's
word: check every residue each names against today's record, with a quotation at the file that decides it; close
what was discharged, re-point the rest to its register row, or mark the arc open by design.

WHAT WAS CHECKED: the fifteen residues the seven name in their own words. Each was looked for across the register,
the leads, the ledgers and the later arcs, and each quotation was found character for character in its file.

  DISCHARGED (5): B1171's time's-arrow instrument (run by B1182); B1171's ask on the R018 numbering gap (R018
    exists and is rowed); B1172's review-carry half (Review 50; the gate on carries); the first OA_SLOW run, for
    B1177 and B1178 (B1207); B1179's send-queue (every item decided HOLD; it stays built and unsent).
  CARRIED (7): Krutelevich's citation (L162, P-332); the MC1 assignment row (P-233); L185's thirteen digest
    rows and its two likeliest reopens (L185); U_e (P-638); the quasinormal channel (P-287, by a reader's
    routing; L189 stays open); the B792 path repairs (P-322, which counts four); the census calls (the queue
    of the remaining mathematics).
  UNREGISTERED (4): no row, lead or later arc decides B1171's zeta-12 / dP6 certificate, B1172's Wave 2 and
    Wave 3 queues (only Wave 3's first item is done, by B1174), B1177's promotion pass (the review item that
    held it closed with B1207, which does not name it; CLAIMS.md has no row of B909 or B952), or B1179's
    cold-pass election. Each is re-pointed to P-745, and P-745's dated addition lists them for main to row or
    to decline.

WHAT CHANGES.
  - Each arc's page gains a dated section: the table of its residues, the outcome, the file read, the
    quotation, and what carries each. Nothing of the page is reworded.
  - B1178, whose one residue is discharged, is closed: its verdict is PROVED from this date, as a process arc
    whose work is done, with a dated bracket at the end of its verdict line that says so and that it states no
    theorem.
  - The six others stay OPEN with a dated marker, ESCALATED(2026-11-13, P-745; carried by ...), beside main's
    marker of 2026-11-10.
  - P-745 gains a dated addition in its next-action cell.

THE LOCK, tests/test_the_seven_process_arcs_checked.py, four tests: each quotation stands in its file (a
quotation changed by one word is not found); each page carries its section, made from the lock's own table,
and the verdicts follow it (B1178 closed, the six OPEN with their marker); the aged-debt check excuses an OPEN
arc only by a marker (each page with its markers taken out is excused by nothing), and does not list the closed
arc; and P-745 names each unregistered residue. On the commit before: 3 failed, 1 passed.

The lock, the seven arcs' own tests, the verdict schema and the tests of the aged-debt and register checks:
1,668 passed. Every gate passes but the count of landings. Not checked by main.
